WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.816 --> 00:00:12.579
The kids were outside doing chores.

2
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.320
The boys were feeding the goats and chickens.

3
00:00:18.121 --> 00:00:19.441
Izzie was picking tomatoes.

4
00:00:21.362 --> 00:00:24.303
Nina's job was to cut basil in the herb garden.

5
00:00:26.143 --> 00:00:28.664
The names of the herbs were printed on wooden signs.

6
00:00:29.832 --> 00:00:31.413
Nina pulled them out of the soil.

7
00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:34.475
"Izzie, look!

8
00:00:35.615 --> 00:00:39.037
These cute signs look like they belong to fairies."

9
00:00:42.159 --> 00:00:42.940
Izzie giggled.

10
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:48.443
"Maybe fairies are in this garden!"

11
00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:54.486
The girls stuck the signs in hidden places where fairies might live.

12
00:00:56.387 --> 00:00:57.488
The boys walked over.

13
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.362
"We're going inside," Bobby said.

14
00:01:01.382 --> 00:01:05.984
"You should come in soon too or Chef will get mad."

15
00:01:07.945 --> 00:01:09.506
The girls collected the signs.

16
00:01:11.427 --> 00:01:13.308
But Nina couldn't remember where they went.

17
00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:16.890
"Uh-oh," she said nervously.

18
00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.772
"Which herb is basil?"

19
00:01:21.073 --> 00:01:21.833
Izzie shrugged.

20
00:01:21.853 --> 00:01:23.994
"I don't know."

21
00:01:25.475 --> 00:01:26.255
Nina gulped.

22
00:01:27.996 --> 00:01:30.118
"I'll just cut a bunch of herbs.

23
00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:33.581
Hopefully, one will be basil."

24
00:01:36.103 --> 00:01:37.524
The girls rushed inside.

25
00:01:39.345 --> 00:01:41.047
Nina put the basket on the counter.

26
00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:44.289
Chef frowned.

27
00:01:44.309 --> 00:01:45.730
"What's this?

28
00:01:47.552 --> 00:01:48.613
I asked for basil!

29
00:01:49.594 --> 00:01:50.674
Why did you bring all these?"

30
00:01:50.694 --> 00:01:57.260
"Uh we Izzie tried to explain.

31
00:01:58.644 --> 00:01:59.405
"I'm sorry!

32
00:01:59.425 --> 00:02:01.346
I mixed up the signs."

33
00:02:02.828 --> 00:02:03.829
Nina hung her head.

34
00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:07.432
"Now you won't know which herbs are which."

35
00:02:09.574 --> 00:02:10.354
Chef laughed.

36
00:02:12.696 --> 00:02:15.218
"Nonsense! I know all the herbs in my garden.

37
00:02:16.359 --> 00:02:18.101
You can learn to identify them too."

38
00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:22.224
He washed the herbs.

39
00:02:24.106 --> 00:02:26.148
Then he set them out in four separate bowls.

40
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.990
"You can identify herbs by the way they look, smell, and taste.

41
00:02:33.211 --> 00:02:35.712
Bobby, take one of these herbs and describe it."

42
00:02:36.693 --> 00:02:38.894
Bobby picked up some long, green strands.

43
00:02:38.914 --> 00:02:44.878
"This herb looks like grass and smells like onions."

44
00:02:46.879 --> 00:02:49.220
"Those are chives," Chef said.

45
00:02:50.581 --> 00:02:52.642
"We use them as a garnish for many dishes.

46
00:02:54.063 --> 00:02:55.384
Now it's Nina's turn."

47
00:02:57.152 --> 00:02:59.113
Nina's herb had shiny, green leaves.

48
00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:03.576
"It smells like pizza!"

49
00:03:05.437 --> 00:03:09.199
"That's the basil we'll use today to make pesto," Chef said.

50
00:03:09.219 --> 00:03:12.301
"We're going to spread it on sandwiches.

51
00:03:13.462 --> 00:03:15.683
It's used in many Italian dishes too."

52
00:03:15.703 --> 00:03:20.486
"Jason and I have the same herb," Izzie said.

53
00:03:21.807 --> 00:03:23.928
Their herb had lots of small leaves.

54
00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.310
"They look alike, but your herbs taste very different.

55
00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.270
Try them," Chef said.

56
00:03:35.092 --> 00:03:38.033
tastes green and peppery," Izzie said.

57
00:03:38.053 --> 00:03:41.655
"That's parsley," Chef said.

58
00:03:43.296 --> 00:03:44.636
Jason nibbled his herb.

59
00:03:44.656 --> 00:03:47.297
"It has a soapy taste."

60
00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:52.760
"It's cilantro, which is used in Mexican and Asian dishes.

61
00:03:54.712 --> 00:03:56.153
These are just four herbs.

62
00:03:57.354 --> 00:03:59.436
You'll get to know them better as you cook more."

63
00:04:01.378 --> 00:04:02.879
It was time to make pesto.

64
00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.662
Nina dumped the basil into the food processor.

65
00:04:08.043 --> 00:04:10.565
Izzie peeled two garlic cloves and added those.

66
00:04:11.946 --> 00:04:13.447
Jason poured in pine nuts.

67
00:04:15.329 --> 00:04:16.970
Bobby turned on the processor.

68
00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.253
It whirred as everything mixed together.

69
00:04:21.754 --> 00:04:24.316
Chef slowly poured in half a cup of olive oil.

70
00:04:26.784 --> 00:04:28.004
He turned off the machine.

71
00:04:28.024 --> 00:04:31.385
"Yum! Smell that basil!"

72
00:04:33.686 --> 00:04:36.947
Jason grated Parmesan cheese and added it to the mixture.

73
00:04:38.807 --> 00:04:40.648
Bobby turned on the processor again.

74
00:04:45.589 --> 00:04:46.610
favorite color!"

75
00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:47.650
Izzie said.

76
00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.751
"It's bright green and smooth!"

77
00:04:52.671 --> 00:04:54.932
Jason spread pesto on slices of bread.

78
00:04:56.968 --> 00:05:00.271
Izzie sliced the tomatoes, and Nina cut up mozzarella cheese.

79
00:05:01.792 --> 00:05:03.473
Bobby put the sandwiches together.

80
00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:07.977
Nina took a bite.

81
00:05:09.117 --> 00:05:10.879
She loved all the different flavors.

82
00:05:10.899 --> 00:05:15.002
"Now I know what basil looks like!

83
00:05:16.203 --> 00:05:19.425
The garden fairies can't trick me ever again!"
